                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15290508" author="roman_s" created="Thu, 19 May 2016 05:54:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vkulichenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vkulichenko&quot;&gt;vkulichenko&lt;/a&gt; Seems you forgot to paste the details of the exception &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/wink.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15306883" author="vkulichenko" created="Mon, 30 May 2016 18:45:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks, Roman! I added the trace.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15320535" author="avinogradov" created="Wed, 8 Jun 2016 13:21:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I wonder how can happen context destroy and then reconnect, except race at node stop.&lt;br/&gt;
Seems that correct solution is to remove &lt;br/&gt;
        if (!initGuard.compareAndSet(true, false))&lt;br/&gt;
            return;&lt;br/&gt;
at onSpiContextDestroyed&lt;br/&gt;
This will fix the problem, I think.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15320679" author="vkulichenko" created="Wed, 8 Jun 2016 14:51:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Anton,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I was under impression that &lt;tt&gt;onSpiContextDestroyed&lt;/tt&gt; can be called on client disconnect. If this is not true, I think you&apos;re right. But the usage of &lt;tt&gt;initGuard&lt;/tt&gt; should be revisited in any case.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15333618" author="avinogradov" created="Thu, 16 Jun 2016 11:38:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
